  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Title, statements of responsibility, publication information from plastic wrapper. One cardboard leaf folded to 48 unnumbered pages in accordion style. Publication date from publisher website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition: 300 Polish, 200 English, including 30 copies of the special edition.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The work was created during the July protests against the judicial reform proposed in 2017 and finally introduced in 2018 by the Law and Justice (PiS) government. The collection of white roses - a symbol of peaceful opposition, stuck in the barriers guarded by the police in front of the Sejm of the Republic of Poland - is banal and accidental. It reminds us of the usual, non-heroic gestures inherent in the protests of the summer of 2017." --Publishers website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
